# A `<send>`'s `idlocation` is a string variable the machine writes the id it
# generates to, which a later `<cancel sendidexpr>` names. Each case takes one
# step away: the analyzer counts it as an engine need again, which the manifest
# of a machine with none would deny; an `id` is admitted beside it, a send
# named twice; it may name a variable that is no string; the id fits a bound one
# byte short of what it needs, whether by the number the judge holds or by how it
